[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4499550486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116751#issuecomment-4499550486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116751","id":4499550486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDDGxFg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T14:44:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T15:10:01Z","body":"> This is an issue for rendering commands relying on the command ordering like CommandAnimationSlice, CommandClipIgnore, CommandTransform.\r\n\r\nProbably should just result in error, since it was not intended for use with commands like this. And in intended use cases order within a single level should not matter.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4499550486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4499783049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116751#issuecomment-4499783049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116751","id":4499783049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDDU9iQ","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T15:10:56Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T04:50:25Z","body":"> Probably should just result in error, since it was not intended for use with commands like this. And in intended use cases order within a single level should not matter.\r\n\r\nActually, no. Transform is used for some RTL effect, so these specific commands should be accounted.\r\n\r\n*Edit: Should be fixed now, these commands are accounted in a separate state and injected as needed after the sort, these do not break batching and simply sorting them as is would defeat most performance benefits.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4499783049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4507193713","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116751#issuecomment-4507193713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116751","id":4507193713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDKZRcQ","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:24:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T10:24:24Z","body":"> *Edit: Should be fixed now, these commands are accounted in a separate state and injected as needed after the sort, these do not break batching and simply sorting them as is would defeat most performance benefits.\r\n\r\nAFAICT should work correctly now, besides the case when `canvas_item_flush_presort` is not called at the end. In such case the relevant CommandAnimationSlice, CommandClipIgnore, CommandTransform simply vanish as `canvas_item_add_set_transform` etc. store their combined state instead of creating actual commands, and then no commands are recreated/reinjected based on the cached states because of no finalizing `canvas_item_flush_presort` call.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Example</summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node2D\r\n\r\n@export var flush_presort := false\r\n\r\nfunc _draw() -> void:\r\n\tvar ci := get_canvas_item()\r\n\tRenderingServer.canvas_item_set_presort_level(ci, 0)\r\n\tvar r := Rect2(Vector2(), Vector2(100, 100))\r\n\tdraw_rect(r, Color.GREEN)\r\n\tdraw_set_transform(r.size)\r\n\tdraw_rect(r, Color.RED)\r\n\tif flush_presort:\r\n\t\tRenderingServer.canvas_item_flush_presort(ci)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`flush_presort  == false`|`flush_presort  == true`\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"godot windows editor dev x86_64_n96bJe9v5d\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d268ad57-061f-4324-b059-a436a58445a4\" />|<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"godot windows editor dev x86_64_YaxLAcqitE\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e2dd7335-78d1-4a47-a768-fafa9edab720\" />\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nNot sure whether this needs to be fixed or just documented but the current note for `canvas_item_set_presort_level` is incorrect:\r\n> If [method canvas_item_flush_presort] is never called, this method has no effect.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4507193713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4507236288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116751#issuecomment-4507236288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116751","id":4507236288,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDKb3wA","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:30:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T10:30:39Z","body":"> Not sure whether this needs to be fixed or just documented but the current note for canvas_item_set_presort_level is incorrect\r\n\r\nRemoved this line from docs, it was already false before the transform/clip/animation change, since it is printing `_cull_canvas_item: Presort list for canvas item XXX was not flushed!` warnings if it's not called.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4507236288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4768857114","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116751#issuecomment-4768857114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116751","id":4768857114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHD78Gg","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https:/